  Add Cats Effect and doobie support alongside the Spring Boot starter:

%{snippet|id=tutorial|file=${basedir}/pom.xml|ignoreDownloadError=false}



*Application class

  The application registers <<<DefaultScalaModule>>> for Jackson serialisation and creates
  a doobie <<<Transactor>>> as a Spring bean using the auto-configured H2 <<<DataSource>>>:

%{snippet|id=tutorial|file=${basedir}/src/main/scala/net/officefloor/tutorial/catshttpserver/Application.scala|ignoreDownloadError=false}



*Cats with doobie

  The <<<MessageRepository>>> issues a SQL query via doobie and returns it as a Cats <<<IO>>>:

%{snippet|id=tutorial|file=${basedir}/src/main/scala/net/officefloor/tutorial/catshttpserver/MessageRepository.scala|ignoreDownloadError=false}



*Service logic

  The <<<service>>> method receives the <<<@RequestBody>>> and the injected <<<Transactor>>>
  (from the Spring bean), runs the doobie query, and returns <<<IO[CatsResponse]>>>.  OfficeFloor
  (via <<<officescala_cats>>>) detects the <<<IO>>> return type, runs it, and passes the result
  as the <<<@Parameter>>> to the <<<send>>> method:

%{snippet|id=service|file=${basedir}/src/main/scala/net/officefloor/tutorial/catshttpserver/ServiceLogic.scala|ignoreDownloadError=false}

%{snippet|id=send|file=${basedir}/src/main/scala/net/officefloor/tutorial/catshttpserver/ServiceLogic.scala|ignoreDownloadError=false}



